  "scientific_limits": {
    "en": "[\"Whole living volume and skin colour are inferred. Sourcefossils are compressed; no false claim of measured live3D proportions.\", \"MainFig8A completes soft contour using real fin/tissue constraints. Remaining fin membrane margins and body flesh are interpretive, not wholly preserved in one photo.\", \"SC1000 andSC1001 are separate same-species individuals; keep numerical measurements distinguished.\", \"Restoration corrects documented small postmortem displacement of caudal soft lobe to its anatomical caudal peak, following authors, not arbitrary fin relocation.\"] {\"unit\": \"metre\", \"nominal_total_length\": 0.985, \"skull_length\": 0.19, \"preorbital_length\": 0.13, \"bony_orbit_ap_width\": 0.041, \"forefin_length\": 0.13, \"hindfin_length\": 0.058, \"dorsal_fin_leading_edge\": 0.068, \"caudal_upper_lobe_height\": 0.043, \"caudal_upper_lobe_leading_edge\": 0.066, \"caudal_upper_lobe_base\": 0.051, \"basis\": \"SOM table forBES SC1000. Forefin approx/incomplete. MainTable1: dorsal leadingedge and caudal height parenthesized/incomplete. Do not label fin leadingedge as verticalheight.\", \"not_measured\": \"Living axial thickness, fin membrane outline between bones, external eye diameter, exact colour, muscular volume. Working maximum body width0.10–0.14m is conservative reconstruction, not a measured living width. Skullorbit41mm is not a41mm protruding eyeball.\", \"source_discrepancy\": \"Use SOM985mm for nominal total, not an exact length inferred from scale of schematicFig8. The schematic guides proportions and fin location, not a photogrammetric replica.\"}",
    "zh": "原创低多边形研究；形态、尺度及不确定性严格以本次已核参考为界。原始限定：[\"Whole living volume and skin colour are inferred. Sourcefossils are compressed; no false claim of measured live3D proportions.\", \"MainFig8A completes soft contour using real fin/tissue constraints. Remaining fin membrane margins and body flesh are interpretive, not wholly preserved in one photo.\", \"SC1000 andSC1001 are separate same-species individuals; keep numerical measurements distinguished.\", \"Restoration corrects documented small postmortem displacement of caudal soft lobe to its anatomical caudal peak, following authors, not arbitrary fin relocation.\"] {\"unit\": \"metre\", \"nominal_total_length\": 0.985, \"skull_length\": 0.19, \"preorbital_length\": 0.13, \"bony_orbit_ap_width\": 0.041, \"forefin_length\": 0.13, \"hindfin_length\": 0.058, \"dorsal_fin_leading_edge\": 0.068, \"caudal_upper_lobe_height\": 0.043, \"caudal_upper_lobe_leading_edge\": 0.066, \"caudal_upper_lobe_base\": 0.051, \"basis\": \"SOM table forBES SC1000. Forefin approx/incomplete. MainTable1: dorsal leadingedge and caudal height parenthesized/incomplete. Do not label fin leadingedge as verticalheight.\", \"not_measured\": \"Living axial thickness, fin membrane outline between bones, external eye diameter, exact colour, muscular volume. Working maximum body width0.10–0.14m is conservative reconstruction, not a measured living width. Skullorbit41mm is not a41mm protruding eyeball.\", \"source_discrepancy\": \"Use SOM985mm for nominal total, not an exact length inferred from scale of schematicFig8. The schematic guides proportions and fin location, not a photogrammetric replica.\"}"
  },
